  "needs_review": null,
  "story": {
    "who": "The sessions are led by Young V&A's Play Champions, according to the venue's own website. The programme was developed with School of Noise, and Play Build Play made its sensory tiles to order; they work on environments with others, with very young children a particular focus, says the venue's own blog.",
    "then": "An earlier run of Sound Explorers started at Young V&A in October 2023, according to the venue's own website, with the same School of Noise collaboration and Play Build Play tiles.",
    "now": "This run belongs to Young V&A's Power of Play programme, which the venue's own website describes as a consortium bringing learning through play to children in Tower Hamlets, funded by the LEGO Foundation.",
    "vibe": "The venue's own website describes it as a chance to listen, play and make noise, using sound and music to explore the museum display.",
    "worth_knowing": [
      "Buggies stay in the designated buggy park, as they cannot go into the Mini Museum space.",
      "Adults take part alongside their children in all Young V&A family activities."
    ],
